course: dictionary
lesson: 11129
title: Words for patterns and spirals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one subject, so the subject gives you the clues. «Fingerprint patterns are loops, whorls and arches» is a science sentence. Loops and arches are also patterns, so a whorl must be a pattern too.
explain: A whorl is a pattern of curved lines that go round and round, like a spiral. To check your meaning, put it in the sentence: «Fingerprint patterns are loops, spirals and arches» still makes sense, so spiral fits.
explain: The same word can also mean a ring or a turn. In a plant, a whorl is a ring of leaves or petals around a stem at one point. On a shell, a whorl is one turn of the spiral. Look at what the text is about to pick the right meaning.
fact: A whorl is a pattern of curved lines that go round and round, like a spiral.
fact: In fingerprints, a whorl is a circle or spiral pattern in the middle of the print.
fact: «Fingerprint patterns are loops, whorls and arches.»
fact: In plants, a whorl is a ring of leaves or petals growing around a stem at the same point.
fact: A whorl on a shell is one turn of its spiral.
exercise: «Fingerprint patterns are loops, whorls and arches.» In this sentence, what is a whorl? | *A kind of fingerprint pattern of curved lines round and round | A type of shoe | A thin line of ink | A kind of fingerprint pattern of curved lines
exercise: «A spindle whorl is a small weight of clay or stone on a stick.» What is a spindle whorl used for? | Cooking soup | *Spinning thread | Catching fish
exercise: In a plant, a whorl is a ring of petals. Where do the petals grow? | Under the soil | *Around a stem at the same point | Inside a shell | At the top of a tree
test: In fingerprints, what is a whorl? | A kind of shoe | A thin line of ink | *A circle or spiral pattern in the middle of the print | A type of bird
test: What is a whorl on a shell? | A crack in the shell | *One turn of the shell's spiral | A hard outer case | The colour of the sea
exam: Read «Fingerprint patterns are loops, whorls and arches; arches are the rarest.» Which pattern is the rarest? | Spirals | Loops | *Arches | Whorls
